Z||000000||Cheever2||04-06-2001||12:11 AM||||I can't believe this.  Search turned up nothing.  Can't check the PFF CD until I get home.  Searched the Net and came up empty handed.  Must not be using the right words.<P>Surely people have considered getting square or rectangular exhaust tips to fit into the cutout shapes on the rear bumper.  Has anybody done this?  Any reason not to?  What cars had them, and where do you get em?<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Oreif||04-06-2001||12:13 AM||||I have seen square/rectangle ones on the mid 90's Grand Prix and always wondered how that would look on the rear of the Fiero. They seem big enough to match the cut-outs of the Fiero. Just never pursued the idea.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-06-2001||12:20 AM||||ive seen tips square and rectangle, even chevy emblew shape at autozone & pepboys. JC Whitney prob has them too. There specialists in weird stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||04-06-2001||12:23 AM||||Borla makes them, they look awesome, I considered them to match my exhaust but they are really expensive IMHO and not worth it.  I have seen them in the summit/jegs mags.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||04-06-2001||02:11 AM||||Any independent muffler shop should stock something like that. I have some on my car. I asked for Megs, but the shop put on some no-name look alikes. But they were about 1/2 the price of Megs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||04-06-2001||06:07 AM||||Dash on down to your local speed shop - they have catalogs with piles of different tips.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||04-06-2001||06:33 PM||||When all else fails look to the GM styles...<P>Take a look around the part yards and ask for Camaro Z-28 exhaust tips. They were rectangular and I have seen them on notchbacks and fastbacks alike. They look PERFECT!<P>A few phone calls and you will have some bad ass exhaust tips!||||reg||6
